8d8_84618f94",30,0,1,"This looks like `kGroupedPrimaryBackgroundColor`. Can we reuse that?"],["ecf1d7c5_eeae4c2d",29,0,1,"Can this be removed ?"]],0,339],[7106320,20405,35,0.385,0.294,[[3,6]],[["",31,-13,1]],0,340],[7146225,20405,191,4.044,3.245,[[0,331]],[["4c8cf682_6e6d6966",0,0,1,"Nit: add a bug number"],["6bc33529_31259493",32,0,1,"same here"],["7ca35fb6_0a5fbf27",0,0,1,"\"attach current tab\" is already allowed with the option to select all tabs, this CLs seems to remove the option when the current tab is already attached"],["87256a53_d03859ff",29,0,1,"WDYT about renaming this to `setCanAttachCurrentTab` ?"]],0,341],[7156812,20406,8,0.451,0.316,[[0,332]],[],0,342],[7154487,20406,472,6.365,5.105,[[0,333]],[["23318804_f54194df",0,0,1,"Can you add a recording ?"],["3f1a1fbc_a2d99064",33,0,1,"This might be an issue as the content after `[self.omniboxTextInputDelegate textInputDidChange:self];` might be different, why do we need to move it above ?"],["4707e4a4_717efba8",34,0,1,"Can this be removed ?"],["86d3a86e_1e958683",29,0,1,"Can these be removed ?"],["cf99fd14_8763e3dc",29,0,1,"Do you think this logic should be in the mediator ? This will also dependent on the DSE, maybe incognito and `IsComposeboxCompactModeEnabled()`"],["e29c27b7_b29facd4",34,0,1,"For this to remain valid with the textfield can you add a case with the textfield ? We can return 1 for example so the API is still valid."],["f901b279_e562cb28",34,0,1,"Add a comment"]],0,343],[7156435,20406,239,4.044,3.245,[[0,0.822,334,197],[6,0.178,0,42]],[["0d5ee3d0_b4b08b4b",35,0,1,"Can you order this red -> green -> blue?"]],0,344],[7156526,20409,56,1.122,0.86,[[0,335]],[["4d148774_e41083e6",36,0,0,"I think we should keep a more general naming, as the bottom position will probably affect more things in the future. (keyboard selection, popup suggestions anchoring, etc..)"]],0,345],[7156567,20409,165,4.044,3.245,[[0,0.793,336,135],[5,0.207,11,28]],[["2ab0b2e3_33fbef20",0,0,1,"458264810, 450966919, 458265654"],["4481f144_4969ae89",29,0,1,"Can we use UIMenu selectedElements for this ? https://developer.apple.com/documentation/uikit/uimenu/selectedelements Maybe it will also put the icons to the right."],["ce2b4314_1c9b807d",0,0,0,"The icons should be on the right of the text."]],0,346],[7170648,20412,86,2.087,1.667,[[0,337]],[["e1825aab_102a2fa2",29,0,1,"```suggestion _glowEffectView = ios::provider::CreateGlowEffect( CGRectZero, kInputPlateCornerRadius, kGlowEffectWidth); ``` If the glow effect is working now, we can re-enable it!"]],0,347],[7178560,20413,307,6.365,5.105,[[0,338]],[["dca1626b_320d4336",37,0,0,"I imagine that this will change depending on the entrypoint. Is this what you had in mind ?"]],0,348],[7181924,20413,43,1.122,0.86,[[0,339]],[["eeeec719_7db0174a",29,0,1,"We should keep the current disabled option for the treatment 3"]],0,349],[7185745,20413,16,0.634,0.471,[[0,340]],[],0,350],[7184960,20413,2,0.147,0.096,[[0,341]],[],0,351],[7185184,20413,56,1.122,0.86,[[0,342]],[["88978ac3_17488787",0,0,1,"Fixed: 461741682"]],0,352],[7186347,20413,8,0.451,0.316,[[0,343]],[],0,353],[7185566,20413,24,0.634,0.471,[[0,344]],[],0,354],[7184981,20416,79,2.087,1.667,[[0,345]],[["b42e50bd_683439cd",29,-3,1,"Should we also update the button state here ?"]],0,355],[7198343,20416,113,2.087,1.667,[[0,0.524,346,59],[6,0.476,1,54]],[["32d0ff12_e3b16dc1",38,0,1,"nit: background"],["6f9804ed_5316df20",0,0,0,"Dark mode doesn't match the mocks: https://www.figma.com/design/z7o7I9f5tDDqI7khMg7TV9/Mobile-Omnibox-AI-Evolution?node-id=3295-116037&t=6qQv1A1meZNtTJXl-0"],["fc483901_d5a0f33e",35,0,1,"Can these 2 be red -> green -> blue?"]],0,356],[7198666,20416,77,2.087,1.667,[[0,347]],[],0,357],[7207276,20419,125,2.087,1.667,[[0,0.956,348,121],[5,0.044,12,4]],[["3128f4bb_681e8902",39,0,1,"They are in the wrong pragma I Think?"],["a25e53da_96a41d06",40,0,1,"Remove this"],["ced69a72_9311008b",29,0,1,"Private method, add comment."],["d9cf7504_16747c03",39,0,1,"Private method. Move it to the correct pragma and add comment"],["f0590671_7f7ca9f8",33,0,1,"Same"]],0,358],[7203350,20420,443,6.365,5.105,[[0,1.0,349,441]],[["5f9f7584_1bbbcdfb",28,-2,1,"There are some event like app stop when the coordinator must be stopped without animations: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:ios/chrome/browser/browser_view/ui_bundled/browser_…"],["956e1740_c94803ff",41,-2,1,"Should this be readonly so we can only update it via the consumer ?"],["39b026e9_93c1ed6e",42,-1,1,"This doesn't seem to be within the described purpose of this protocol, since it doesn't provide views or other properties for the animation."],["401e2bca_0ff3084d",42,-1,1,"Nit: \"Provider\" seems like a word we don't need here. I know we often name protocols \"provider\", but by definition most interfaces, especially ones that are mostly readonly properties, provide…"],["5b08da13_118e7ef1",41,-1,1,"Follow Objc naming/calling conventions for boolean properties: - The property name *does not* have a predicate (\"is\" or \"has\"). - The getter should have a predicate prefix. I would also suggest that…"],["750ccaac_015addbf",28,-1,1,"Please mark which API these methods belong to -- `#pragma mark - ComposeboxAnimationContextProvider`. They should come before the private methods."],["7fd49e42_32905bc2",28,-1,0,"Really this coordinator shouldn't be digging into the properties of other coordinators' view controllers. My suspicion is that ComposeboxCoordinator and ComposeboxInputPlateCoordinator are both…"],["a4578a67_02160409",28,-1,1,"Why not something like this ? ```suggestion [_viewController.presentingViewController dismissViewControllerAnimated:animated completion:completion }]; ```"],["ad81def4_ba487998",37,-1,1,"It looks like this call to -stop is what ensures that the composebox coordinator does its cleanup, which feels brittle. The fact that -stop will internally call `-dismissAnimated:completion:` a…"],["c63f836b_3742958f",43,-1,0,"If you pass a ProceduralBlock type here the callback should be bind repeating. Otherwise, it might crash if it's called multiple times."],["d7e3d93e_57a63a6e",37,-1,0,"It need to be changed here then"],["f6c6f094_d04e6462",44,-1,1,"you can just name this _animationBase or even just _base, it's perfectly clear in context."],["585d0410_6424ad98",37,0,1,"This just needs to nil the cooordinator, not also call -stop, right?"]],0,359],[7205545,20420,156,4.044,3.245,[[0,350]],[["83b22bce_5e63d7a2",29,0,1,"```suggestion buttonConfig.image = SendButtonImage(/*highlighted=*/NO); ```"],["cae52492_597ff568",29,0,1,"```suggestion /// Configures the menu items for the plus (+) button. ```"]],0,360],[7213151,20423,186,4.044,3.245,[[0,351]],[],0,361],[7210928,20423,13,0.451,0.316,[[0,352]],[],0,362],[7222970,20425,3,0.147,0.096,[[0,353]],[["8e6b013b_b5647eb8",19,0,1,"Should this behavior also apply with a normal textfield?"]],0,363],[7217029,20425,403,6.365,5.105,[[0,354]],[["177956cf_bca1b820",32,0,1,"Optional nit: I'd remove `IfNeeded`, as we are always updating the consumer compact mode."],["189799b4_370d46f7",32,0,1,"This method can be removed entirely? In the block line 231, just call updateButtonsVisibility."],["1ef42430_8568d92e",45,0,1,"Nit: could be forward declared."],["21868d0a_ca3992c0",46,0,0,"Is this related to the rest of the CL?"],["33458d33_d597e294",32,0,1,"I'd remove this call from here. This should be called explicitly by the caller when the conditions of compactModeRequired change."],["8a76bc6d_28362ece",47,0,1,"(Optional nit: `this->` is unnecessary, IIANM?)"],["ae65f536_ef4291ab",32,0,1,"Drive-by: we might be missing a call to updateConsumerActionsState and updateConsumerItems here?"],["b14780ee_b258b60b",29,0,0,"This seems not directly related to this CL?"],["bcf8ca6e_d4e1fa79",47,0,0,"What about directly leveraging equality? That way we check all at once and get a better error log. ```suggestion EXPECT_EQ([consumer_.visibleControls, ComposeboxInputPlateControls::kVoice |…"]],0,364],[7223210,20425,22,0.634,0